This year we will be offering an in-person full day ctmm workshop, "Introduction to continuous-time movement modeling for animal tracking data", at The Wildlife Society's 29th Annual Conference on Sunday, Nov 6th, 08:00 AM - 05:00 PM.

There will also be a talk on RSF-informed AKDE later in the week.

The conference will be held November 6-10 in Spokane, Washington, and the early bird discount runs out at the end of this month:  twsconference.org <https://twsconference.org/?utm_source=getresponse&utm_medium=email&utm_campaign=current_members_tws&utm_content=Early%20registration%20for%20TWS%20Annual%20Conference%20ends%20July%2031%21>

